></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal">Ledwell, J.L., and R.W. Aldrich. <year>1999</year>. Mutations in the S4 region isolate the final voltage-dependent cooperative step in potassium channel activation. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>113</volume>:<fpage>389</fpage>&#x02013;414.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10051516</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Long, S.B., E.B. Campbell, and R. Mackinnon. <year>2005</year>. Crystal structure of a mammalian voltage-dependent Shaker family K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channel. <source>Science.</source> <volume>309</volume>:<fpage>897</fpage>&#x02013;903.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16002581</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Mannuzzu, L.M., M.M. Moronne, and E.Y. Isacoff. <year>1996</year>. Direct physical measure of conformational rearrangement underlying potassium channel gating. <source>Science.</source> <volume>271</volume>:<fpage>213</fpage>&#x02013;216.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8539623</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Melman, Y.F., A. Domenech, S. de la Luna, and T.V. McDonald. <year>2001</year>. Structural determinants of KvLQT1 control by the KCNE family of proteins. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>276</volume>:<fpage>6439</fpage>&#x02013;6444.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11104781</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Melman, Y.F., A. Krumerman, and T.V. McDonald. <year>2002</year>a. A single transmembrane site in the KCNE-encoded proteins controls the specificity of KvLQT1 channel gating. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>277</volume>:<fpage>25187</fpage>&#x02013;25194.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11994278</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Melman, Y.F., A. Krummerman, and T.V. McDonald. <year>2002</year>b. KCNE regulation of KvLQT1 channels: structure-function correlates. <source>Trends Cardiovas